museRISC muserisc_bext — AES S-box rework: synthesis before/after (2026-10-15)
==========================================================================

Tools (Docker image openroad/orfs:latest,
sha256:63981d1ac8990a9bee8bf874c95ee2c1ee3fe7b99f57d459282ab8c31a8ed663,
created 2026-10-11):
  Yosys 0.68+post, OpenROAD (OpenSTA) from the same image,
  sv2v v0.0.13 (SV -> Verilog-2005 front end for Yosys),
  Nangate45 NangateOpenCellLibrary_typical.lib.

Flow (per variant):
  sv2v muserisc_bext_pkg.sv muserisc_bext.sv -w bext.v
  yosys: read_verilog bext.v; hierarchy -check -top <top>;
         synth -flatten -top <top>; dfflibmap -liberty LIB;
         abc -D 10000 -liberty LIB; opt_clean -purge;
         stat -liberty LIB; write_verilog -noattr netlist.v
  yosys: read_liberty -lib LIB; read_verilog netlist.v; ltp -noff
         (logic depth = longest topological path, in cells)
  openroad/OpenSTA: virtual 10 ns clock, input/output delay 0,
         report_checks -path_delay max. Two figures:
         "raw"    = unbuffered mapped netlist (high-fanout op
                    decode nets dominate),
         "repair" = after initialize_floorplan + setRC +
                    repair_design (fanout/slew buffering and
                    resizing only, no placement, no wires).
  The unit is purely combinational, so every path is
  input port -> output port.

1. Original RTL (origin/main 896e88c) — NOT SYNTHESIZABLE
---------------------------------------------------------
  gf_inv() computes x^254 with a `while (e > 0)` loop around
  8 chained variable x variable gf_mul() calls. Yosys:

    bext.v:156: ERROR: Function \muserisc_bext_pkg_gf_inv can
    only be called with constant arguments.

  For a before/after comparison the while loop was rewritten
  by hand, outside the repo, as the equivalent constant-bound
  loop (`for i in 0..7: if (254 >> i) & 1 then r = gf_mul(r,
  base); base = gf_mul(base, base)`), i.e. exactly the
  circuit the original describes once it can be unrolled.
  That "original (unrolled)" variant is the baseline below.

2. Full muserisc_bext unit
--------------------------
  variant                    yosys   cells   area um2  ltp  STA raw  STA repair
  original (while loop)      ERROR   -       -         -    -        -
  original (unrolled equiv)  15:53   45,293  55,156    89   8.077 ns 6.961 ns
  this PR (GF((2^4)^2))      1:17    18,795  22,786    60   3.957 ns 2.497 ns
  alt: 256-entry case LUTs   1:20    22,606  26,591    64   3.501 ns 2.461 ns

  (yosys = wall clock of the synthesis run; area = Yosys
  `stat -liberty` chip area; repaired area is within 0.2%.)

  Area -59% (55,156 -> 22,786 um2), critical path -64%
  (6.961 -> 2.497 ns after buffering; 87 -> 32 cells), and the
  synthesis run itself goes from ~16 min to ~1.3 min.

  Critical path, this PR (after repair_design), 32 cells:
    op_i[4] -> op decode (NOR3_X4, fanout 135: S-box
    direction / ks1i select) -> S-box input mux -> input
    matrix XORs -> GF(16) arithmetic + GF(16) inverse ->
    GF(16) multiplies -> output matrix -> MixColumns XORs ->
    result mux -> result_o[37]. 2.497 ns, slack 7.503 ns at
    10 ns.
  Original (unrolled, after repair_design): op_i[3] ->
    result_o[2], 87 cells, 6.961 ns: the eight-deep chain of
    GF(2^8) multipliers inside each S-box.

  The ltp of 60 in the new unit is no longer the AES path: it
  is the 64-bit ripple-carry adder that ABC maps for the
  Zba sh*add / add.uw `+` (AOI21/OAI21 carry chain from
  a_i[2]), which STA shows is not the critical path (cells
  ~25-40 ps each). Left alone: a `+` is the right RTL; a
  faster adder is a mapping choice (e.g. ORFS ADDER_MAP),
  not an RTL defect.

3. One S-box lane (forward + inverse, as instantiated 8x)
--------------------------------------------------------
  Wrapper: y = aes_sbox_fi(x, inv) (original: inv ?
  aes_isbox(x) : aes_sbox(x)).

  variant                    area um2  ltp  STA (raw = repair)
  original (unrolled equiv)  3,537     82   6.042 / 5.741 ns
  this PR (GF((2^4)^2))        313     17   1.074 ns
  alt: 256-entry case LUTs     793      8   0.518 ns

  Design choice: composite field. Per lane it is 2.5x smaller
  than the LUT pair (one inverter shared by both directions
  vs. two 256-entry tables), and the unit-level critical path
  is within 0.04 ns of the LUT variant (2.497 vs 2.461 ns)
  because the S-box is only part of the AES path (input mux,
  MixColumns, result mux). Both are far inside a 10 ns cycle
  and stay single-cycle. The LUT halves S-box depth but costs
  +3,800 um2 (+17%) for the unit.

4. Other loops / deep chains reviewed (no change needed)
---------------------------------------------------------
  - gf_mul in mixcol/imixcol: only constant second operands;
    folds to xtime/XOR networks (synthesized fine above).
  - clmul128: constant 64-iteration loop -> AND array + XOR
    trees; ABC rebalances; not on the critical path.
  - clz64/ctz64 (priority loops), cpop (`cnt +=` loop), SHA
    sigma/sum (fixed rotates/XOR), xperm4/8 (mux trees):
    constant-bound and synthesizable; none on the critical
    path above.
  - The only unsynthesizable construct was the while loop in
    gf_inv (plus its early `return`): Yosys only evaluates such
    functions for constant arguments. Removed.
